# Git LFS — binary assets go to LFS by default.
#
# The rule is "by extension, anywhere", not "by directory": the point is that
# dropping a new texture, model or screenshot in needs no thought and no edit
# here. `git add` applies the clean filter and the blob lands in LFS.
#
# Two things depend on this and fail *silently* if LFS is not fetched, so they
# are worth knowing before adding a pattern:
#
#  1. **Some of these are `include_bytes!`-ed at compile time** — the brand font
#     (`assets/fonts/*.ttf`, see `systems::theme`), the app icon
#     (`assets/icon/cartopolis.png`), the star catalog (`assets/sky/*.bin`) and the
#     routing/tile/vegetation test fixture (`crates/cartopolis/tests/fixtures/*.mvt`).
#     Without the smudge filter those are 130-byte pointer files and the build
#     happily embeds the pointer: the font panics in epaint, the icon doesn't
#     decode, the fixture tests run on garbage. Every `actions/checkout` in
#     `.forgejo/workflows/` therefore sets `lfs: true`, and a fresh clone needs
#     `git lfs install` (see `assets/README.md`).
#  2. **`docs/img/*.png` is regenerated wholesale** by `cargo shots`. That is the
#     highest-churn binary in the repo — ~10 MB of screenshots rewritten whenever
#     the chrome changes — and exactly what LFS exists for.
#
# Adding a pattern does not move blobs already in history; it applies from the
# next commit that touches the file. `git add --renormalize .` converts the ones
# already tracked, in one ordinary commit.

# 3D models and their buffers
*.gltf  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.glb   filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.bin   filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
# The avatar body pack (`crates/human`, `human-pack`).
*.humanpack filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# Images: source textures, the app icon, and the generated `docs/img` set
*.png   filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.jpg   filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.jpeg  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.ico   filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.webp  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.ktx2  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.dds   filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.hdr   filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.exr   filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# Fonts
*.ttf   filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.otf   filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.woff2 filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# Audio
*.ogg   filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.wav   filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.mp3   filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# Map data fixtures (a vector tile is protobuf, not text)
*.mvt   filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.pbf   filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
